{
  "abstract": "We report here the first observation of directed flow ($v_1$) of the hypernuclei $^3_{\\Lambda}$H and $^4_{\\Lambda}$H in mid-central Au+Au collisions at $\\sqrt{s_{\\rm NN}}$ = 3 GeV at RHIC. These data are taken as part of the beam energy scan program carried out by the STAR experiment. From 165 $\\times$ 10$^{6}$ events in 5%-40% centrality, about 8400 $^3_{\\Lambda}$H and 5200 $^4_{\\Lambda}$H candidates are reconstructed through two- and three-body decay channels. We observe that these hypernuclei exhibit significant directed flow. Comparing to that of light nuclei, it is found that the midrapidity $v_1$ slopes of $^3_{\\Lambda}$H and $^4_{\\Lambda}$H follow baryon number scaling, implying that the coalescence is the dominant mechanism for these hypernuclei production in such collisions.",
  "access_urls": {
    "links": {
      "csv": "https://www.hepdata.net/download/submission/ins2605845/1/csv",
      "json": "https://www.hepdata.net/download/submission/ins2605845/1/json",
